menu "UltraWideLock UWB round"

    # The menuconfig face of the same two knobs a project can set as CMake
    # variables before project.cmake (the CMake variable wins; see
    # CMakeLists.txt). Names, ranges and defaults mirror
    # modules/ultrawidelock_uwb/Kconfig so a value carries between the Zephyr
    # lock and this port unchanged.

    config ULTRAWIDELOCK_NUM_RESPONDERS
        int "Responder count the CCC round is built for"
        range 1 2
        default 1
        help
            Number_Responder_Nodes advertised in M3 and baked into the
            RangingConfiguration SaltedHash (cred_round_config.h). Every image
            in the session -- lock AND satellite -- must be built with the same
            value, or every derived STS/dURSK/dUDSK diverges and nothing
            decodes. 1 = validated 1:1 baseline; 2 = dual-anchor round with a
            second responder transmitting Response_1.

    config ULTRAWIDELOCK_RESPONDER_INDEX
        int "This node's responder index in the round"
        range 0 1
        default 0
        help
            Which Response slot this build transmits in: responder l replies
            at POLL + 1 + l slots / STS index + 1 + l. 0 is the lock, 1 is the
            satellite. Must be unique per node and less than
            ULTRAWIDELOCK_NUM_RESPONDERS (compile-enforced in
            cred_round_config.h).

endmenu
